BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Davis Farmers Market - Every Saturday from 8am - 1pm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T010000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T060000
UID:10001850-1793433600-1793451600@davisdowntown.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the heart and soul of Davis every Saturday at the 
 Davis Farmers Market in Central Park! \n🗓 Every Saturday⏰ 8:00 AM 
 – 1:00 PM📍 Central Park\, Davis \nShop fresh from the source with lo
 cal farmers and vendors offering: \n🥕 Fresh\, seasonal produce🌻 Farm
  products🛍 Handmade crafts🥖 Fresh-baked goods☕ Coffee and hot food
  \nWhether you’re stocking up on locally grown ingredients\, enjoying br
 eakfast in the park\, or simply soaking in the vibrant community atmospher
 e\, the Davis Farmers Market is a beloved weekly tradition for all ages. \
 nBring your family\, support local growers and makers\, and enjoy the boun
 ty of our fertile region every Saturday!
LOCATION:Central Park\, 301 C St.\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United States
URL:https://davisdowntown.com/event/davis-farmers-market-every-saturday-fr
 om-8am-1pm/2026-10-31/
X-SOURCE:Davis Downtown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zombie Bike Parade
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T040000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T053000
UID:10002205-1793444400-1793449800@davisdowntown.com
DESCRIPTION:The Zombie Bike Parade Everyone is welcome at Community Park f
 or the festival: on foot\, on any wheels\, in a wheelchair or powerchair\,
  or pushing a stroller. The official bike parade is different. It rides ju
 st under five miles at a regular biking pace\, so it is for bicycles (incl
 uding e-bikes\, cargo bikes\, tandems and bike trailers) and only for ride
 rs who can keep that pace for the whole route. Helmets are required under 
 18 and strongly encouraged for everyone. If the parade is not the right fi
 t\, stay at Community Park: the shows\, the entertainment stations and the
  2:30 p.m. skydiving finale all happen there.
LOCATION:Community Park\, 203 E 14th St\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United Stat
 es
URL:https://davisdowntown.com/event/zombie-bike-parade/
X-SOURCE:Davis Downtown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Davis Downtown Treat Trail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T100000
UID:10002206-1793458800-1793466000@davisdowntown.com
DESCRIPTION:Two full hours collecting candy at dozens of downtown business
 es. Start at Davis Commons\, where TOMO Tea House\, Bruxie\, Mom’s Dumpl
 ing\, Mikuni\, Shabu Shack\, Xfinity\, and My Burma are all handing out sw
 eets\, then carry on into the rest of downtown.
URL:https://davisdowntown.com/event/davis-downtown-treat-trail/
X-SOURCE:Davis Downtown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Día de Muertos: Day of the Dead Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T110000
UID:10002215-1793548800-1793559600@davisdowntown.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Día de Muertos (Day of the Dead) in Downtown Davis!
  \nJoin the community at E Street Plaza for a vibrant celebration honoring
  loved ones\, culture\, and tradition. Enjoy an afternoon and evening fill
 ed with colorful altars\, live entertainment\, traditional music\, dancing
 \, and family-friendly activities. \nEvent Highlights: \n\n12:00 PM – 7:
 00 PM: Altars and ofrendas honoring loved ones\n4:00 PM – 7:00 PM: Welco
 me celebration\, folklórico dance performances\, mariachi music\, and liv
 e band entertainment\nFace painting\, community booths\, and local vendors
 \n\nBring your family and friends to experience the beauty and traditions 
 of Día de Muertos while celebrating community and culture in the heart of
  Downtown Davis! \nLocation: E Street Plaza\, Davis\, CA \nDate: Sunday\, 
 November 1\, 2026 \nMain Celebration: 4:00 PM – 7:00 PM \nPresented in p
 artnership with local community organizations and supported by the Davis C
 hamber of Commerce\, Davis Phoenix Coalition\, and community sponsors.
URL:https://davisdowntown.com/event/dia-de-muertos-day-of-the-dead-celebra
 tion/
X-SOURCE:Davis Downtown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Davis Odd Fellows Classic Film Fest: One\, Two\, Three
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T130000
UID:10002211-1793557800-1793566800@davisdowntown.com
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for an evening of classic comedy as the Davis Odd Fe
 llows Classic Film Fest returns with a special series celebrating the scre
 wball comedies of the 1960s and 1970s! \nThe series kicks off with One\, T
 wo\, Three (1961)\, Billy Wilder’s fast-paced political comedy starring 
 James Cagney\, Horst Buchholz\, and Arlene Francis. \nDavis Enterprise fil
 m critic Derrick Bang will introduce the film with behind-the-scenes insig
 hts and fun facts\, followed by a Q&A after the screening. Enjoy live musi
 c by According to Bazooka before the movie! \nAdmission and popcorn are FR
 EE! Donations are welcome\, and the bar will be open for beverage purchase
 s. \nDoors open at 6:29 PM\, and the movie begins at 7:01 PM. Everyone is 
 welcome!
LOCATION:Davis Odd Fellows\, 415 2nd St.\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United Sta
 tes
URL:https://davisdowntown.com/event/davis-odd-fellows-classic-film-fest-on
 e-two-three/
X-SOURCE:Davis Downtown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Munchie Man: Grand Opening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T023000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T130000
UID:10002216-1793701800-1793739600@davisdowntown.com
DESCRIPTION:There’s a new spot in Downtown Davis! Join us on November 3 
 to celebrate the grand opening of Munchie Man! \nThe festivities kick off 
 with a special ribbon-cutting ceremony hosted by the Davis Chamber of Comm
 erce at 10:30 AM\, followed by doors opening to the public at 11:00 AM. \n
 Come welcome Munchie Man to the downtown community and check out Davis’ 
 newest addition! \nLearn more: www.munchiemandavis.com \n \nMunchie Man st
 arted as a 2023 pop-up in East Sacramento and now in 2026 we are a “funk
 y bistro” specializing in local craft beer & wine with small plates. \nE
 verything you’ll find here tells a story. The menu is inspired by my tra
 vels\, the restaurants that left an impression on me\, and the people and 
 experiences that shaped who I am. In many ways\, it’s an autobiography t
 old through food. Some dishes are inspired by places I’ve visited\, othe
 rs by people I love\, and a few simply exist because they make me smile. A
 nd I hope they make you smile too.
URL:https://davisdowntown.com/event/munchie-man-grand-opening/
X-SOURCE:Davis Downtown
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Davis Farmers Market – Wednesday Evenings (50th Anniversary Year
 )
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T180000
UID:10002135-1793804400-1793815200@davisdowntown.com
DESCRIPTION:The Davis Farmers Market continues every Wednesday in Central 
 Park with new fall hours! \nBeginning Wednesday\, September 2\, the Wednes
 day market will be open from 3:00–6:00 PM\, replacing the extended 4:00
 –8:00 PM Picnic in the Park hours. \nStop by to shop for fresh\, locally
  grown produce\, artisan goods\, prepared foods and other market favorites
  from local farmers and vendors. It’s a great opportunity to stock up fo
 r the week\, meet up with friends\, support local growers and food makers\
 , and enjoy a beautiful afternoon in Central Park. \nThe Davis Farmers Mar
 ket is celebrating its 50th Anniversary in 2026\, marking five decades of 
 bringing fresh food\, local farmers and the Davis community together. \nWe
 dnesday Market Details: \n\nWednesdays from 3:00–6:00 PM\nCentral Park i
 n Downtown Davis\nFresh\, seasonal produce\nArtisan goods and prepared foo
 ds\nLocal farmers and food makers\nFamily-friendly and open to everyone\n\
 nFree to attend – shop local and enjoy your Wednesday afternoon at the D
 avis Farmers Market!
LOCATION:Central Park\, 301 C St.\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United States
URL:https://davisdowntown.com/event/davis-farmers-market-year-round-fresh-
 local-in-central-park-50th-anniversary-year-2-3-2/2026-11-04/
X-SOURCE:Davis Downtown
END:VEVENT
